senses
  entry
    definition "the phonological or orthographic sound or appearance of a word that can be used to describe or identify something"
    examples ("the inflected forms of a word can be represented by a stem and a list of inflections to be attached")
    id oewn-06301417-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms ("word form" signifier descriptor)
  entry
    definition "a category of things distinguished by some common characteristic or quality"
    examples ("sculpture is a form of art" "what kinds of desserts are there?")
    id oewn-05847533-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (kind sort variety)
  entry
    definition "a perceptual structure"
    examples ("the composition presents problems for students of musical form" "a visual pattern must include not only objects but the spaces between them")
    id oewn-05939522-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (shape pattern)
  entry
    definition "any spatial attributes (especially as defined by outline)"
    examples ("he could barely make out their shapes")
    id oewn-05071206-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (shape configuration contour conformation)
  entry
    definition "alternative names for the body of a human being"
    examples ("Leonardo studied the human body" "he has a strong physique" "the spirit is willing but the flesh is weak")
    id oewn-05224424-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms ("human body" "physical body" "material body" soma build figure physique anatomy shape bod chassis frame flesh)
  entry
    definition "the spatial arrangement of something as distinct from its substance"
    examples ("geometry is the mathematical science of shape")
    id oewn-00028005-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (shape)
  entry
    definition "the visual appearance of something or someone"
    examples ("the delicate cast of his features")
    id oewn-04684871-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (shape cast)
  entry
    definition "a printed document with spaces in which to write"
    examples ("he filled out his tax form")
    id oewn-06485234-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "(biology) a group of organisms within a species that differ in trivial ways from similar groups"
    examples ("a new strain of microorganisms")
    id oewn-08128123-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (variant strain var.)
  entry
    definition "an arrangement of the elements in a composition or discourse"
    examples ("the essay was in the form of a dialogue" "he first sketches the plot in outline form")
    id oewn-07106984-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "a particular mode in which something is manifested"
    examples ("his resentment took the form of extreme hostility")
    id oewn-04937655-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "(physical chemistry) a distinct state of matter in a system; matter that is identical in chemical composition and physical state and separated from other material by the phase boundary"
